humbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":320,"height":322,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Second_half_19th_century_Shirvan_Kilim.png/960px-Second_half_19th_century_Shirvan_Kilim.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/Second_half_19th_century_Shirvan_Kilim.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_half_19th_century_Shirvan_Kilim.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=113096460","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2021-12-05 22:05:08","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"Second half 19th century Shirvan Kilim","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Kilims|Caucasian carpets and rugs|Shirvan (historical region)|PD-Art (PD-old-100)|Files uploaded by PDTillman|CC-PD-Mark|19th-century textiles|PD-Art missing SDC copyright status|PD-old missing SDC copyright status","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This second half 19th century Shirvan Kilim measures 5\u20192\u201d X 10\u20195\u201d (158 x 320 cm). This is a lovely Kilim. The wider bands are all on an ivory ground with hooked medallions. The pink color is doubtless from East Turkestan where you don\u2019t see a lot of kilims of this age. The thinner bands are probably cochineal or madder red and plain. In the bottom ivory band on the left side there is a construction of geometric shapes and at the top there are two figures that look like men with hats. Maybe they are, maybe they are not. On the back of the kilim there is a fabric sleeve for hanging. This rug probably didn\u2019t see much time on the floor. All in all, this is a very interesting piece. The condition is very good except for some small holes the size of a dime that could be stitched up.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"second half 19th century","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://antique-rugs.jozan.net/antique-shirvan-kilim-rug-52-x-105-7878/\">https://antique-rugs.jozan.net/antique-shirvan-kilim-rug-52-x-105-7878/</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Unknown Shirvan weavers. Photo by seller, Robert T. Mosby","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<table cellspacing=\"8\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-interactive, #f0f0f0); color: inherit; border: 2px solid var(--border-color-subtle, #e0e0e0); width:100%;\" class=\"layouttemplate\" dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>\n<div class=\"center\">This is a faithful photographic reproduction of a two-dimensional, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Public_domain\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Public domain\">public domain</a> work of art. The work of art itself is in the public domain for the following reason:</div>\n<div dir=\"auto\">\n<table class=\"licensetpl\" style=\"display:none\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span class=\"licensetpl_short\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_long\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_link_req\">false</span><span class=\"licensetpl_attr_req\">false</span>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; clear: both; margin: 0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-progressive-subtle, #f7f8ff); color: var(--color-base, #202122); border: var(--border-subtle, 2px solid #8888aa); border-spacing: 8px; padding: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"layouttemplate\" lang=\"en\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span title=\"Public domain\"><img alt=\"Public domain\" src=\"https://thumb