\"><a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/deed.en\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"ccorg:publicdomain/mark/1.0/deed.en\">This file has been identified as being free of known restrictions under copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights.</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table><span class=\"licensetpl_link\" style=\"display:none;\">https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/</span><span class=\"licensetpl_short\" style=\"display:none;\">PDM</span><span class=\"licensetpl_long\" style=\"display:none;\">Creative Commons Public Domain Mark 1.0</span><span class=\"licensetpl_link_req\" style=\"display:none;\">false</span><span class=\"licensetpl_attr_req\" style=\"display:none;\">false</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"center\">The official position taken by the Wikimedia Foundation is that \"<i>faithful reproductions of two-dimensional public domain works of art are public domain</i>\".<br><b>This photographic reproduction is therefore also considered to be in the public domain in the United States.</b> In other jurisdictions, re-use of this content may be restricted; <b>see <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:Reuse_of_PD-Art_photographs\" title=\"Commons:Reuse of PD-Art photographs\">Reuse of PD-Art photographs</a> for details.</b></div> \n</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"97120009":{"pageid":97120009,"ns":6,"title":"File:Unknown Unidentified Object (FindID 969915).jpg","index":6,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":3032807,"width":3553,"height":2926,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg/330px-Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":320,"thumbheight":264,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg/960px-Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg/330px-Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":320,"height":264,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg/960px-Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/66/Unknown_Unidentified_Object_%28FindID_969915%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unknown_Unidentified_Object_(FindID_969915).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=97120009","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2020-11-29 10:09:05","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"<div class=\"fn\">\nUnknown Unidentified Object</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Portable Antiquities Scheme|Images uploaded by F\u00e6|Portable Antiquities Scheme, SWYOR|Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation (53\u00b0 N, 2\u00b0 W)","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"53.710400","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"-1.901380","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nWest Yorkshire Archaeology Advisory Service, Ian Whitehead, 2019-09-15 13:58:32</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"A Post Medieval probable pipe stopper dating from AD 1700 - 1950 in the form of a hook. The object is 40.5mm long and 21.6mm wide. It is 8.9mm in diameter tapering to a rounded point and it weighs 7.12g. The material is not entirely obvious. Thought at first to be ivory or bone, close examination of a chipped area reveals a closely textured, solid, granular material, with a gritty feel, suggested to be ceramic (perhaps pipeclay). It is also possible that it is a modern synthetic material such as resin, bakelite or plastic.<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<p>It is a rod of circular cross-section, with a tapering hook at one end. The other end is nearly flat and is discoloured to a dark brown. An area of brown staining extends along the hook shaft for about 7mm. The rest of the hook is a cream / buff colour with dark brown speckles. There is a line along the back of the hook, extending up the full length of the shaft where the speckles are more closely spaced, possibly the very well trimmed remains of a casting seam.</p>\n<p>The discolouration may be caused by adhesive material, suggesting that there was an attachment at the wider end which is now missing. The attachment could have taken the form of a metal ferrule with a loop for suspension on a chain.</p>\n<p>The hook is worn on the inner face of the hooked area, to a glossy finish, which extends up the full length of the shaft on that face. The wear is more pronounced on one side of the hook (the left side if the discoloured end is uppermost, and the hook curves towards the viewer).</p>\n<p>Some possible parallels for hooked and curved pipe stoppers can be seen on page 100 (plate 109) of Leslie (2012) 300 Years of Tobacco Stoppers; Fine Works of Art in Miniature. These have rather wider curves and usually have a silver ferrule on the wider end which was used as the stopper. The pointed end is sometimes used as a picker and can also have a silver tip.</p>\n<p>If the object is not a pipe tamper or stopper, the wear could suggest that the hook was used for a practical function, possibly for textile working or net making, but it is larger and of a different shape to crochet hooks, and different to hooks for making rag rugs. It could also be a button hook, but it seems unusually large. It could work as a handle for a miniature umbrella or parasol, perhaps for a doll, but it seems unlikely that a toy would have the amount of wear that is present on this example.</p>\n<p>This object was originally recorded as a possible pendant in the form of a hook, possibly replicating a bone fish-hook, and probably of Modern date.</p>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"between 1700 and 1950<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1500-00-00T00:00:00Z/6,P1319,+1700-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1326,+1950-00-00T00:00:00Z/9</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://finds.org.uk/database/ajax/download/id/1072717\">https://finds.org.uk/database/ajax/download/id/1072717</a><br>Catalog: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://finds.org.uk/database/images/image/id/1072717/recordtype/artefacts\">https://finds.org.uk/database/images/image/id/1072717/recordtype/artefacts</a> <bdi lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\" title=\"archived on 29 November 2020 at the Wayback Machine\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20201129100808/https%3A//finds.org.uk/database/images/image/id/1072717/recordtype/artefacts\">archive copy</a> at the <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Wayback Machine\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">Wayback Machine</span></a></span></bdi><br>Artefact: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/969915\">https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/969915</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"Attribution License","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Attribution":{"value":"West Yorkshire Archaeology Advisory Service","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-2.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]}}}}